{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917515446},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Use a dataset about farmers markets \n2. Use a census file with population data\n3. Calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Express the answer to four decimal places\n5. Provide one confident sentence\n6. Use tools to do the math, not manual calculation\n7. Not mention unverified facts\n\nAccording to the project instructions for the xorq analyst, I need to:\n1. First check for semantic models (`xorq_semantic_models`) and catalog aliases\n2. Never ingest data without checking if it already exists in the catalog\n3. Use `xorq_select` to get values from the catalog\n4. Use `xorq_verify` to verify every number I'm going to state\n5. Never do math myself - compose it into the catalog as an alias\n\nLet me start by:\n1. Orienting with `xorq_semantic_models` and `xorq_catalog_list_aliases`\n2. If the data isn't in the catalog, I'll need to ingest it using a build script\n3. Create aliases for both datasets\n4. Create a derived metric alias that calculates per capita\n5. Query the result and verify it\n\nLet me begin by checking what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the answer using the xorq catalog and verified tools. Let me start by checking what's already in the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Q5zKt1zicJTSqzG7iXFPiW","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01XCY5roghuDPJ1SgVTN7dKF","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":439,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8306,"totalTokens":8755,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0021950000000000003,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0103825,"total":0.0125875},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":293},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786917515459,"responseId":"msg_011Ce7BE2LKU4MMAvgxXWoJ9","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Q5zKt1zicJTSqzG7iXFPiW","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"us_markets  (model: us_markets)\n  dimensions: state, state_abbr\n  measures:   markets, residents, markets_per_100k\n\nRead a measure with xorq_semantic_select (measures=['<measure>']).\nPick the measure that answers the question DIRECTLY — never fetch component\nmeasures and combine them by hand: hand arithmetic fails verification.\nA measure queried with NO dimensions is already the model's GRAND TOTAL\n(full reviewed scope) — do not aggregate, compose, or re-derive it."}],"details":[{"alias":"us_markets","name":"us_markets","dimensions":["state","state_abbr"],"measures":["markets","residents","markets_per_100k"]}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786917520989},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01XCY5roghuDPJ1SgVTN7dKF","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"us_markets   ← SEMANTIC MODEL (measures: markets, residents, markets_per_100k)\n\nA semantic model's measures are reviewed metric definitions — read them by name with xorq_semantic_select (schema via xorq_semantic_schema); never re-derive them.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786917520989},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! The semantic model `us_markets` already exists in the cat